# .env.example — every environment variable the toolkit's code reads, with what it does.
#
# Nothing here is required: each variable has a working default (shown, or "unset" when the code
# treats unset specially). Copy the lines you need into your shell profile or a local, untracked
# .env; this repo never loads a .env file by itself. Never put a real secret in this file.
#
# Checked by scripts/check-env-example.sh (ENV-EXAMPLE-001..004; the bash suite
# scripts/tests/check-env-example.test.sh runs it in CI): a variable the code reads must be listed here, or
# in scripts/env-scan-ignore.txt when the OS, the shell, a host tool or CI sets it. An entry marked
# "(indirect: …)" is read through a configured name or by a tool, so the scan can't see it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# State and install locations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Root of all toolkit state (judge, sindri, scorer, locks, digests, proof). The hooks and the TS packages
# read it.
# AW_STATE_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow

# The C# Sindri app (src/Sindri, not installed until the switch). Its state directory: ledger.db, approvals,
# control.json and logs. Default $AW_STATE_DIR/sindri-app, apart from the TS sindri's $AW_STATE_DIR/sindri.
# Also read by the Sindri app (sindri-ui), which finds control.json and auth/human.token here and keeps its own state
# in ui/ (preferences.json and the single-instance files; docs/csharp/sindri-ui.md).
# AW_SINDRI_HOME=~/.agentic-workflow/sindri-app
# Set by the launcher on a launched agent session (never by hand): the launch id (config/hooks/session-id-report.sh also reads it and
# writes that session's own id to $AW_SINDRI_HOME/launches/<id>.session-id; scripts/install-meta.sh installs the hook for Codex and
# Cursor) and the item it is for. `sindri session wrap` proves its heartbeat and exit calls with the launch secret, which reaches
# it as a path, never as a value: AW_SINDRI_LAUNCH_SECRET_FILE names the 0600 one-read file launch/secrets/<id>.secret under
# $AW_SINDRI_HOME. Wrap reads it once, deletes it and sets AW_SINDRI_LAUNCH_SECRET in the agent's environment only (never argv, never a file).
# AW_SINDRI_LAUNCH=
# (indirect: AW_SINDRI_ITEM is passed on by name in Host/Commands/SessionWrap/WrapEnvironment.cs)
# AW_SINDRI_ITEM=
# AW_SINDRI_LAUNCH_SECRET_FILE=
# The program the launcher runs `session wrap` with inside a launched session. Default: the running sindri; `sindri` on the PATH when
# Sindri runs under `dotnet run` (the process is then the dotnet host).
# AW_SINDRI_EXE=
# AW_SINDRI_LAUNCH_SECRET=

# The session launcher's machine file (Sindri and aw-meta-launch; docs/csharp/sindri-launcher.md): the terminal viewer, the
# tmux or none host, extra agent catalog entries and the Meta lanes' agents. Default $AW_STATE_DIR/launcher.json
# Read by scripts/launcher-lib.sh (aw-meta-launch, its lanes); the C# Sindri launcher reads it from SL-2.
# AW_LAUNCHER_CONFIG=~/.agentic-workflow/launcher.json

# The session collector (docs/csharp/sindri-sessions.md; Sindri's SessionCollectorHost). AW_FLEET_DIR is where the aw:fleet hook
# writes one state file per session and the collector reads and prunes them. Default $AW_STATE_DIR/fleet.
# AW_FLEET_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/fleet
# AW_FLEET_DISABLE=1 makes the aw:fleet hook (config/hooks/fleet-state.sh) write nothing in that session; unset by default.
# AW_FLEET_DISABLE=1
# TEST OVERRIDES, tests and the prover's fixture tree only: AW_SESSIONS_PROC_ROOT replaces /proc and AW_SESSIONS_CLAUDE_DIR replaces
# launcher.json's sessions.claudeSessionsDir (default ~/.claude/sessions). Either one shows an informational SND-SESSION-003 problem
# row beside the normal list, turns the pruning of hook files off and makes focus answer copy only.
# AW_SESSIONS_PROC_ROOT=/proc
# AW_SESSIONS_CLAUDE_DIR=~/.claude/sessions

# The C# Sindri app's profile file. Default <AW_SINDRI_HOME>/profile/profile.yaml.
# AW_SINDRI_PROFILE=~/.agentic-workflow/sindri-app/profile/profile.yaml

# The denylist of work identifiers that scripts/denylist-check.sh reads, injected as a pointer, never a path in code or
# briefs: file:<absolute path> (a regular file, mode 0600 or stricter, owned by you) or env:<VAR> (newline-separated
# entries in that variable). Anything else, a bare path included, is refused and the check fails closed (exit 2).
# Set it in your own environment; agents never open the list. Prefer file:; export an env: variable only in the shell
# that runs the check, never in a shell that launches an agent (its environment would hold the identifiers).
# AW_DENYLIST=

# The C# Sindri app's loopback API port; overrides the approved profile's api.port (default 7410). 0 picks a free port.
# (indirect: LoopbackBinding.PortVariable in src/Sindri/Aw.Sindri.Host/LoopbackBinding.cs)
# AW_SINDRI_PORT=7410

# The Temporal namespace and task queue the C# Sindri app uses (README X61): serve's dev server creates the namespace,
# its worker polls the queue, and instances start on it. Each defaults to 'sindri'.
# AW_SINDRI_TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE=sindri
# AW_SINDRI_TEMPORAL_TASK_QUEUE=sindri

# Registers the test-only Step input 'input.prove.echo' (a proof drives it; its text is <home>/prove/echo.txt and its call log
# <home>/prove/echo.log). Honoured only when the home is a prover home (inside the temp directory or a proof folder).
# AW_SINDRI_PROVE_BLOCKS=0
# The directory of an exported tracker (issues.json and projects.json) that 'step.scope.read-tracker' reads through the file tracker adapter. Unset: no tracker is configured and the Step fails with SND-SCOPING-005.
# AW_SINDRI_TRACKER_DIR=
# Where the docker CLI sends its commands (read by `sindri onyx`, which refuses anything but a local unix socket or named pipe: SND-ONYX-010). Unset: the current docker context.
# DOCKER_HOST=

# The Sindri app binary that bare `sindri` opens (S1b, docs/csharp/sindri-ui.md). Default: sindri-ui next to the sindri binary.
# (indirect: UiLauncher.Variable in src/Sindri/Aw.Sindri.Host/Commands/UiLauncher.cs)
# AW_SINDRI_UI=

# Hard cap, in whole seconds, on one sindri CLI call to the running control plane (docs/csharp/sindri.md). Unset or 0: no
# cap, so a slow but healthy answer completes; connecting is always bounded at 5 s. Over 2147483 or non-numeric is SND-CLI-003.
# (indirect: CliTimeout.Variable in src/Sindri/Aw.Sindri.Host/Commands/CliTimeout.cs)
# AW_SINDRI_CLI_TIMEOUT=0

# scripts/sindri-app.sh (`sindri-app`, the C# Sindri in one command): 1 skips linking ~/.local/bin/sindri-app (or
# CLAUDE_LOCAL_BIN/sindri-app) to the script. Default 0: linked from the canonical checkout.
# AW_SINDRI_APP_NO_LINK=0
# 1 makes scripts/sindri-app.sh skip registering Sindri's MCP with the installed providers once the control plane is up
# AW_SINDRI_APP_NO_MCP=0
# The profile repo name scripts/sindri-app.sh passes to `sindri mcp register --repo` (default: the repo the directory is in; a linked worktree passes its main checkout's name)
# AW_SINDRI_MCP_REPO=

# The claude executable 'sindri mcp register --apply' runs (C# Sindri). Default: claude on PATH. Tests and proofs point it
# at a recording stub so no real provider config is written.
# AW_SINDRI_CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# (indirect: the launcher sets them for the agent, which reads them) Set in an unattended Step's session (scoping-station spec W11, L-17(b)); never set by hand. The workflow
# instance address the Step belongs to, and the Step directory the agent reads its facts from and writes its outputs to.
# AW_SINDRI_INSTANCE=
# AW_SINDRI_RUN_DIR=
# (indirect: the launcher sets it for the agent, which reads it) The Step's worktree, set for an unattended agent Step (line spec LN-LCH1). The pre-push hook Sindri
# installs there refuses a push wherever it is set. The launcher also blanks GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN and AW_FORGE_TOKEN for the Step and
# points GH_CONFIG_DIR at an empty directory; never set by hand.
# AW_SINDRI_WORKTREE=

# The C# Sindri CLI's command line for scripts/sindri-prove.sh (split on spaces). Unset: dotnet run --project
# src/Sindri/Aw.Sindri.Host --. Point it at a built binary for proofs; never the TS `sindri` on PATH.
# SINDRI=
# scripts/sindri-ui-fixture.sh stall: the event type of the unparseable row it inserts. Unset: service.ran.
# STALL_TYPE=
# scripts/sindri-ui-fixture.sh items: the repo the fixture's items are added to. Unset: the API's default.
# FIXTURE_REPO=

# Alias for AW_STATE_DIR in the provider installers (providers/lib.sh); AW_STATE_DIR wins when both are set.
# AW_STATE_ROOT=~/.agentic-workflow

# Where the Codex and Cursor hook scripts are installed (Claude's: CLAUDE_HOOKS_DIR below).
# AW_HOOKS_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/hooks

# Where the scorer's launchd job plist is written (macOS; install-sindri.sh always uses ~/Library/LaunchAgents).
# AW_LAUNCH_AGENTS_DIR=~/Library/LaunchAgents

# Directory the CLI wrappers (judge, sindri, scorer) are installed into.
# CLAUDE_LOCAL_BIN=~/.local/bin

# The toolkit checkout the Claude hook installer links from (default: this repo). setup.sh always sets it
# to its own checkout, so a value here only applies when providers/claude/install-hooks.sh runs directly.
# TOOLKIT_DIR=

# Claude Code's config directory and settings file, as the Claude installer sees them.
# CLAUDE_DIR=~/.claude
# SETTINGS_FILE=~/.claude/settings.json

# Cursor's config directory, as the Cursor installer sees it.
# CURSOR_DIR=~/.cursor

# Per-provider hook targets for the hook installer (config/hooks/adapters/install-lib.sh).
# CLAUDE_HOOKS_DIR=~/.claude/hooks
# CLAUDE_SETTINGS_FILE=~/.claude/settings.json
# Also read by the C# sindri doctor's context:mcp-scope row ($CODEX_HOME/config.toml) and by Sindri's Codex usage reader ($CODEX_HOME/sessions, the launch budgets).
# CODEX_HOME=~/.codex
# CODEX_HOOKS_FILE=~/.codex/hooks.json
# CURSOR_HOOKS_FILE=~/.cursor/hooks.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# setup.sh and installers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1 = answer "y" to every installer prompt (non-interactive installs).
# AW_ASSUME_YES=0

# 1 = build the Serena C# / Swift LSP image even when setup.sh finds no .cs/.csproj or .swift files (it
# builds them automatically when it does).
# BUILD_CSHARP=0
# BUILD_SWIFT=0

# 1 = skip registering launchd jobs (scorer, sindri) on macOS.
# AW_SKIP_LAUNCHD=

# 1 = install-sindri.sh writes the wrapper only (dist/ already built; used by tests).
# AW_SKIP_BUILD=0

# The sindri source checkout install-sindri.sh builds from (default: this repo).
# AW_SINDRI_SRC=

# 1 = don't install the prompt-sort hook (Claude and Codex).
# AW_NO_PROMPT_SORT=0

# The judge binary the install scripts call.
# AW_JUDGE_BIN=judge

# scripts/dotnet-verify-packages.sh: the dotnet executable to use.
# DOTNET=dotnet

# aw-readiness: the gh executable it runs for the repo's remote settings.
# AW_READINESS_GH=gh

# Every C# host (aw-readiness, aw-packets, packages from /new-package): the lowest Kernel telemetry level written to
# stderr as JSON lines: trace, debug, information, warning, error, critical or none. An unknown value writes one
# AW-TELEMETRY-001 warning and logs at information (indirect: src/Aw.Kernel.Telemetry/TelemetryOptions.cs LevelVariable).
# AW_LOG_LEVEL=information

# bugfix-state (src/BugFix): seconds a run-test command may run before it is killed and counted as failing (default
# 1800) (src/BugFix/Aw.BugFix.Infrastructure/BugFixSettings.cs).
# AW_BUGFIX_CHECK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800
# bugfix-state: seconds a call waits for another call's state lock before refusing with AW-BUGFIX-021 (default 30)
# (src/BugFix/Aw.BugFix.Infrastructure/BugFixSettings.cs).
# AW_BUGFIX_LOCK_WAIT_SECONDS=30
# bugfix-state: extra variables a test command needs (comma-separated names, e.g. DATABASE_URL,JAVA_HOME), passed to it
# and frozen with the check like PATH and HOME; loader and shell-startup names (BASH_ENV, NODE_OPTIONS, PYTHON*, LD_*, …)
# are never passed (src/BugFix/Aw.BugFix.Infrastructure/BugFixSettings.cs).
# AW_BUGFIX_CHECK_ENV=
# .NET's switch that turns file locks off. bugfix-state refuses to change state while it is set (AW-BUGFIX-022), since
# its state lock would no longer keep two calls apart (src/BugFix/Aw.BugFix.Infrastructure/BugFixSettings.cs). Leave unset.
# DOTNET_SYSTEM_IO_DISABLEFILELOCKING=

# scripts/ci/bash-tests.sh: how many suites run at once (default: the CPU count).
# BASH_TESTS_JOBS=
# scripts/ci/bash-tests.sh: the repo root to run in (its own tests point it at a fixture tree).
# BASH_TESTS_ROOT=
# scripts/ci/bash-tests.sh: newline-separated suites to skip, replacing its built-in list.
# BASH_TESTS_EXCLUDED=
# scripts/ci/bash-tests.sh: newline-separated suites to run one at a time, replacing its built-in list.
# BASH_TESTS_SERIAL=

# scripts/owner-check.sh --seed: the merged build's sindri command, which exports the real map for an owner check.
# SINDRI_MAIN=
# scripts/owner-check.sh: the scratch instance's port in place of 7480; its tests only (scripts/tests/owner-check.test.sh).
# OWNER_CHECK_PORT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hooks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fail-open log: the largest log file before it rotates, in bytes.
# AW_FAILOPEN_MAX_BYTES=1048576

# context-guard: its config directory, its state directory, and the growth gate in bytes.
# AW_CONTEXT_GUARD_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/context-guard
# AW_CONTEXT_GUARD_STATE_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/context-guard/state
# AW_CONTEXT_GUARD_GROWTH_GATE_BYTES=20000

# done-gate: where judge session files are read.
# AW_JUDGE_SESSIONS_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/judge/sessions

# outbox-flush: the judge outbox directory.
# AW_OUTBOX_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/judge/outbox

# record-teammate-name: the teammate-name table.
# AW_TEAMMATE_NAMES_FILE=~/.agentic-workflow/judge/teammate-names.jsonl

# probe-log: where the hook-input probe writes (scripts/probe.sh on|off).
# AW_PROBE_DIR=~/.agentic-workflow/probe

# prompt-sort and sindri-nudge: time budget per call, in milliseconds.
# AW_PROMPT_SORT_BUDGET_MS=1500
# AW_SINDRI_NUDGE_BUDGET_MS=1500

# prism-context: the prism-mcp dashboard port it checks.
# PRISM_DASHBOARD_PORT=7180

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Statusline
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Seconds before the live cache is refreshed.
# AW_STATUSLINE_LIVE_TTL=15

# Non-empty = print the width it chose (and why) to stderr.
# AW_STATUSLINE_DEBUG=

# Test overrides: the tty to measure, and the command that reports its columns.
# AW_STATUSLINE_TTY=
# AW_STATUSLINE_TTY_COLS_CMD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# judge
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Comma-separated provider allowlist (the --providers flag wins). Unset: every provider. An empty value is an
# error (judge exits 64), so leave the line commented unless it names providers.
# AW_JUDGE_PROVIDERS=

# The judge's own directory (decisions.sqlite, config.json), used as is instead of $AW_STATE_DIR/judge. For a caller that
# runs its own judge with its own store (Sindri); it moves nothing else, locks and other tools' state stay under AW_STATE_DIR.
# AW_JUDGE_STATE_DIR=

# The calling session's id, recorded with decisions.
# AW_SESSION_ID=

# API key for the prompt-sort provider; the macOS keychain is used when unset. Leave empty here.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sindri
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Directory holding the sindri profile (unset: the <state root>/profile link that `sindri profile init`
# creates; no link and no variable means no profile).
# AW_PROFILE_DIR=

# The box-wide heavy-job lock (builds, test runs, index builds). Slot 1 is this path, slot k is this path
# plus ".k"; each slot is a mkdir mutex (config/lib/locks.sh).
# AW_HEAVY_JOB_LOCK=~/.agentic-workflow/locks/heavy-job.lock
# How many heavy jobs may run at once (slots of the lock; a whole number >= 1). Unset or empty means 1 in the heavy wrapper
# and Sindri's C# build; config/lib/locks.sh's callers (the ui-evidence skill and scaffold e2e.sh pass ${AW_HEAVY_SLOTS:-2}), the
# C# Evidence port, the TS sindri lock and new-package/new-slice use 2 when it is unset. A value that is
# not a whole number of at least 1 (`two`, `0`, `-1`) means 1 in the wrapper (and for AW_SESSION_HEAVY_SLOTS), in locks.sh (so in its
# callers) and in Sindri's C# build, and 2 (the default, with a notice in the Evidence port) in the C# Evidence port, the TS sindri lock
# and new-package/new-slice. A padded value such as " 3" is read as 3 by the trimming readers (Evidence, the TS lock, the scaffolds) and as 1
# by locks.sh and Sindri's C# build; write the number with no spaces.
# AW_HEAVY_SLOTS=1

# The sindri binary the generated pre-commit hook calls.
# SINDRI_BIN=sindri

# 1 = print scrubbed stack traces on errors.
# SINDRI_DEBUG=

# Word list for derived-privacy checks.
# SINDRI_WORDS=/usr/share/dict/words

# A secret pointer "env:NAME" in a sindri profile reads NAME at use (indirect: sindri/src/secrets.ts);
# the name is the profile's choice, so it is not listed here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# scorer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `scorer audit --label` passes only these to the claude child it starts (indirect: scorer/src/audit/claude-runner.ts).
# Leave them empty here; claude's own login normally covers it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Also read by the C# sindri doctor's context:mcp-scope row ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.claude.json) and by Sindri's Claude Code usage reader ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects, the launch budgets).
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# aw-live mod
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The scorer binary the /live pane runs (unset: ~/.local/bin/scorer, then scorer on PATH).
# AW_SCORER_BIN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ui-evidence
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The local config file and the app title the doctor checks. The C# `ui-evidence doctor` reads the file
# only when UI_EVIDENCE_CONFIG names it (indirect: src/Evidence/Aw.Evidence.Features/Doctor/DoctorService.cs).
# The TypeScript skill and doctor.sh also read a committed skills/ui-evidence/deployment.env (absent here;
# a fork adapting the toolkit to one app commits its own), below the local file in precedence.
# UI_EVIDENCE_CONFIG=skills/ui-evidence/.ui-evidence.local.env
# UI_EVIDENCE_APP_TITLE=

# The regex a preview --host's whole hostname must match; unset refuses every non-local host
# (indirect: src/Evidence/Aw.Evidence.Features/RunScript/RunScriptService.cs, Parity/ParityService.cs).
# UI_EVIDENCE_PREVIEW_HOST_PATTERN=pr-[0-9]+\.preview\.example\.com

# A localhost API port the doctor must reach; unset skips the check.
# UI_EVIDENCE_API_PORT=

# A git worktree whose stack slot the doctor checks; default: the current worktree.
# UI_EVIDENCE_WORKTREE=

# The worktree slot convention: the slot file in a worktree's root and the NAME in it holding N, the highest
# slot, the port step (slot N serves web on 3000+STEP*N), the slot database name with {slot}. Unset: no slots.
# The runner reads the count and step through named constants (indirect: skills/ui-evidence/src/host-guard.ts slotConfig).
# UI_EVIDENCE_SLOT_FILE=
# UI_EVIDENCE_SLOT_KEY=
# UI_EVIDENCE_SLOT_COUNT=
# UI_EVIDENCE_SLOT_PORT_STEP=
# UI_EVIDENCE_SLOT_DATABASE=

# The Docker container running the local Postgres and its user, for the doctor's pg_isready and the
# provenance query; no container skips the doctor's database check and leaves provenance unknown.
# UI_EVIDENCE_DB_CONTAINER=
# UI_EVIDENCE_DB_USER=postgres

# DB provenance: the [schema.]table whose email column is read (unset: provenance unknown), comma-separated
# seed domains and a seed-email pattern
# (indirect: src/Evidence/Aw.Evidence.Features/CheckProvenance/CheckProvenanceService.cs).
# UI_EVIDENCE_SEED_TABLE=
# UI_EVIDENCE_SEED_DOMAINS=example.com
# UI_EVIDENCE_SEED_EMAIL_PATTERN=seed-admin-%@example.com

# Browser user agent override (indirect: src/Evidence/Aw.Evidence.Features/RunScript/ScriptRun.cs, Parity/ParityRun.cs).
# UI_EVIDENCE_USER_AGENT=

# A label for the visual-check model in the verdict-cache key: change it to invalidate cached visual
# verdicts. It does not select the model (`judge visual-critique` does)
# (indirect: src/Evidence/Aw.Evidence.Features/RunScript/RunVerdict.cs).
# AW_VISUAL_MODEL=judge-default

# The box-wide lock on the local app stack.
# AW_QA_STACK_LOCK=~/.agentic-workflow/locks/qa-stack.lock

# Seconds a skill waits for its session lock (skills/_shared/skill-lock.sh).
# SKILL_LOCK_TIMEOUT=120

# The event type `stall` writes into the scratch ledger (scripts/sindri-ui-fixture.sh); default service.ran.
# STALL_TYPE=service.ran

# A manifest's login names its own email and password variables (indirect: skills/ui-evidence/src/host-guard.ts);
# those names are per app, so they are not listed here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent identity (scripts/agent-token.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The GitHub App and installation the token is minted for (unset: the toolkit's own App and installation,
# whose ids are in scripts/agent-token.sh), and the API base (tests only: the script accepts
# https://api.github.com or a loopback URL).
# AGENT_APP_ID=
# AGENT_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
# AGENT_APP_API_URL=https://api.github.com

# The App's private-key file (unset: read from the macOS keychain).
# AGENT_APP_KEY_FILE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Readiness and C# build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# scripts/readiness-baseline.mjs: timeout for each gh call, in milliseconds.
# READINESS_GH_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# The .NET SDK location (indirect: read by the dotnet host, not by repo code). Unset: the directory of the
# dotnet executable. Set it only for a dotnet-install.sh install, e.g. ~/.dotnet.
# DOTNET_ROOT=

# 1 = no CLI telemetry; 1 = no first-run banner (indirect: read by the dotnet CLI). Unset, the CLI sends
# telemetry and prints the banner; CI and the devcontainer set both to 1.
# DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=
# DOTNET_NOLOGO=
# true = verify NuGet package signatures on restore (off by default on macOS; spec §4d) (indirect: read by NuGet).
# DOTNET_NUGET_SIGNATURE_VERIFICATION=
# 1 = no Avalonia build telemetry (indirect: read by Avalonia.BuildServices, which the Avalonia pins bring in). Unset,
# its AvaloniaStats build step would post build statistics to avaloniaui.net; Directory.Build.targets already replaces
# that step with an empty one, and CI and the devcontainer set this to 1 as well.
# AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=

# Sindri UI rev-8 design tools (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-sindri-ui-screens-design/tools): where the
# click-throughs and DOM checks load the prototype and the mockups. Unset: the local static server on 127.0.0.1:8766.
# PROTO_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8766/prototype.html
# MOCK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8766/mockups/

# scripts/install-deps.sh (setup.sh): test-only overrides. AW_DEPS_OS fakes `uname -s` (Linux or Darwin); AW_DEPS_ZLIB_H
# is the zlib.h path checked for the NativeAOT prerequisite (default /usr/include/zlib.h).
# AW_DEPS_OS=
# AW_DEPS_ZLIB_H=

# config/lib/sys-pkg.sh (setup.sh, scripts/install-deps.sh): 1 = never install system packages (no brew, no sudo); print
# the exact install command and fail instead. For CI and boxes you don't administer.
# AW_NO_SYSTEM_INSTALL=

# scripts/sindri-ui-fixture.sh: "python" runs the fixture's ledger SQL through python3's sqlite3 module even when the sqlite3 CLI is installed (without the CLI it is the fallback anyway).
# SINDRI_UI_FIXTURE_SQL=

# scripts/install-deps.sh test-only overrides: AW_DEPS_BWRAP_PROBE is the command that proves bwrap can sandbox
# (default `bwrap --ro-bind / / true`); AW_DEPS_USERNS_FILE is the AppArmor sysctl file read when it fails.
# AW_DEPS_BWRAP_PROBE=
# AW_DEPS_USERNS_FILE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Meta harness (/meta, aw-meta; docs/csharp/meta.md). Installed by ./setup.sh --with-meta (Claude Code only).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The team config (team, repo, lanes, gate scopes, merge order, known flakes, prompts). Default
# $AW_STATE_DIR/meta/teams/<team>/team.json (the legacy flat $AW_STATE_DIR/meta/team.json while no team is selected);
# `aw-meta team-init` writes it.
# AW_META_CONFIG=
# AW_META_TEAM (below, in the lane variables) also selects the team for any aw-meta command, hook or launcher; `--team <name>` does the
# same. With one team on disk, or a legacy config, none is needed; with several and none selected a command exits 2 (AW-META-019).
# The team's state directory (meta.db, lane-sessions/, gates/), exported into every lane by scripts/meta-lane.sh for the lane hooks.
# AW_META_DIR=
# The aw-meta binary the meta hooks and the launcher call. Default $AW_STATE_DIR/bin/aw-meta.
# AW_META_BIN=
# Where aw-meta looks for live Claude Code sessions (<pid>.json files). Default ~/.claude/sessions.
# AW_CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR=
# The heavy-job wrapper aw-meta puts in front of a gate step marked "heavy" (used only when the file exists).
# Default $AW_STATE_DIR/bin-r1b/heavy.
# AW_HEAVY=
# The GitHub CLI program aw-meta calls (tests point it at a stub). Default gh.
# AW_GH=
# scripts/meta-lane.sh: the claude command (default claude) and extra arguments for every lane (default none:
# setup.sh sets permissions.defaultMode to bypassPermissions so every lane runs in the same mode).
# AW_META_CLAUDE=
# AW_META_CLAUDE_ARGS=
# scripts/meta-launch.sh and meta-lane.sh: the lane variables set in every lane's environment (never in tmux's global one):
# AW_META_TEAM is the team, AW_META_LANE the lane, and AW_SINDRI_CHILD=1 marks the session as a Sindri child so a
# `sindri` run inside it is a session caller. Lane-side hooks and commands (SL-1b) take the lane from these and nothing else.
# AW_META_TEAM=
# AW_META_LANE=
# Set by scripts/meta-lane.sh in every lane: its own pid (the parent of the lane's agent), the agent's catalog id and its process name.
# The Codex and Cursor lane hooks (config/hooks/meta-lane-gate.sh, session-id-report.sh) act only under the lane's own agent: not without
# AW_META_LANE_PID, not in a Claude lane, not in a codex exec or cursor-agent -p the agent started itself.
# AW_META_LANE_PID=
# AW_META_LANE_AGENT=
# AW_META_LANE_PROC=
# 1 = scripts/meta-launch.sh starts the team's lanes even when sessions of the same names still run on tmux's default socket
# (the pre-switch team); same as --allow-legacy. Default: it refuses, so no lane runs twice.
# AW_META_ALLOW_LEGACY=
# scripts/meta-launch.sh: the `tmux -L` socket to check for those old sessions instead of tmux's default one (tests use a private one).
# AW_META_LEGACY_TMUX_SOCKET=
# aw-meta-launch warns (one stderr line) when the installed aw-meta is older than this checkout's Meta sources; 1 skips that check.
# AW_META_NO_STALE_CHECK=
# Seconds scripts/meta-launch.sh and meta-lane.sh wait for an agent that reports its own session id (default 30; tests).
# AW_META_ID_WAIT=
# Seconds a lane whose id did not arrive in time keeps the start lock, waiting for its late session file (default 10; tests).
# AW_META_ID_GRACE=
# aw-meta stop-check's loop guard (and lane-stop-check's, for a non-Claude lane's reply): how many re-blocks (stops with stop_hook_active)
# the same open obligations get in one turn, after the first block, before the stop is let through with a warning (default 3)
# (indirect: read through ConsoleIo.Env in StopCheckCommand.cs and LaneStopCheckCommand.cs).
# AW_META_STOP_MAX=
# The tmux program aw-meta lane-send uses to look at a non-Claude lane's pane and wake it (default tmux).
# Tests point it at a stub. It always runs with `-L`: the team's own socket (`-L <team>`), or AW_META_TMUX_SOCKET when set.
# AW_TMUX=
# The tmux socket name aw-meta passes as `-L` instead of the team's own (default: `-L <team>` from team.json). Tests and proofs set a unique one.
# AW_META_TMUX_SOCKET=
# 1 = scripts/meta-lane.sh exits when claude exits instead of dropping to a shell (tests).
# AW_META_NO_SHELL=
# scripts/meta-launch.sh: where the Warp launch configuration is written. Default
# ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/warp-terminal/launch_configurations.
# AW_WARP_LAUNCH_DIR=
# XDG_DATA_HOME=
# 1 = setup.sh leaves permissions.defaultMode in ~/.claude/settings.json alone (default: sets bypassPermissions,
# so cross-session messages between lanes aren't held for a mode mismatch).
# AW_NO_CLAUDE_BYPASS=
# src/Meta/aot-smoke/run.sh: run the smoke against this aw-meta binary instead of publishing one (debugging the smoke).
# AW_META_SMOKE_BIN=
# scripts/test-tmux.sh (tests only): the tmux socket name the helper uses for ttmux and its PATH shim; default t1-<pid>-<random>, a test may preset the name of the team it runs.
# AW_TEST_TMUX=
# scripts/test-tmux.sh (tests only): the helper's temp directory (set by the helper; holds TMUX_TMPDIR and the tmux shim).
# AW_TEST_TMUX_DIR=
# aw-forge-fake / Aw.Forge.Host (docs/csharp/forge.md): which forge adapter to use, file (the default) or github.
# AW_FORGE_ADAPTER=
# aw-forge-fake: the allowed forge hosts, a comma list. Default forge.test for the file adapter, github.com for github.
# AW_FORGE_HOSTS=
# aw-forge-fake: where the forge credential comes from, env:NAME (a variable holding a token) or command:<argv>
# (a program run per call that prints a token). Default env:AW_FORGE_TOKEN. The credential itself is never in config.
# AW_FORGE_CREDENTIAL=
# The forge token the default credential source reads (a GitHub token for the github adapter). Never logged or printed.
# The login the file-backed forge acts as (the author of its replies; Self answers it). Default sindri.
# AW_FORGE_LOGIN=
# AW_FORGE_TOKEN=
# Aw.Forge.Tests heavy lane (GitHubForgeContractTests): owner/name of a scratch GitHub repository the read-side contract
# runs against; skipped unless this and AW_FORGE_TOKEN are both set.
# AW_FORGE_GITHUB_REPO=
# Aw.Forge.Tests heavy lane (GitHubForgeWriteContractTests): 1 also runs the write contract (it pushes two branches and opens a
# pull request in AW_FORGE_GITHUB_REPO, then deletes the branches). Anything else skips it.
# AW_FORGE_GITHUB_WRITE=
# scripts/forge-fixture.sh: where the PR babysitter's fixture PR set is built (the repositories and the file-backed fake forge world).
# Must be inside the temp folder or a proof folder; default ${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/aw-forge-fixture-<uid>.
# FORGE_FIXTURE_HOME=
# scripts/forge-fixture.sh: the aw-forge-fake command line (split on spaces) to use instead of building src/Forge/Aw.Forge.Host into <home>/bin.
# AW_FORGE_FAKE=
# scripts/forge-fixture.sh up --github <owner/repo>: set to the same owner/repo to confirm it is a scratch repository (the owner's step).
# FORGE_FIXTURE_GITHUB_SCRATCH=
# sindri scoping desk evidence (docs/csharp/sindri-scoping.md): the aw-packets program that hashes the assembled scope packet; default aw-packets on the PATH.
# AW_PACKETS_BIN=
# sindri bugfix block Steps (docs/csharp/sindri-workflow.md): the bugfix-state program they run; default bugfix-state on the PATH.
# AW_BUGFIX_BIN=
# scripts/install-onyx.sh (setup.sh --with-sindri): the sindri-app it runs `onyx up` through; default scripts/sindri-app.sh in this checkout (tests point it at a stub).
# AW_ONYX_SINDRI_APP=
# scripts/install-onyx.sh: 1 treats the run as being at a terminal (tests only; a real run asks the shell).
# AW_ONYX_FORCE_TERMINAL=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh (aw-headroom claude|codex): the upstream the client would use without headroom, first hit wins; headroom's own URL never counts.
# Claude reads ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, then settings.json env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL; Codex reads OPENAI_BASE_URL, then the active provider's base_url in config.toml.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh: loopback ports of the headroom proxies it starts (defaults 8791 for Claude, 8792 for Codex).
# AW_HEADROOM_PORT_CLAUDE=
# AW_HEADROOM_PORT_CODEX=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh: the headroom executable; default headroom on PATH, then ~/.local/bin/headroom.
# AW_HEADROOM_BIN=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh: 1 leaves the proxy running after the last wrapped session exits (default: it is stopped).
# AW_HEADROOM_KEEP=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh: seconds to wait for the proxy's /health before running the tool unwrapped (default 120).
# AW_HEADROOM_START_WAIT=
# scripts/aw-headroom.sh: extra arguments for `headroom proxy`, split on spaces.
# AW_HEADROOM_ARGS=
# scripts/install-headroom.sh: where the aw-headroom launcher is installed (default ~/.local/bin).
# AW_HEADROOM_BIN_DIR=
# scripts/install-headroom.sh: the pip requirement installed when headroom is missing (default headroom-ai[proxy]).
# AW_HEADROOM_PACKAGE=
# scripts/ci/recipe-versions.sh: the command that runs sindri, split on spaces (default: dotnet run --no-build --configuration Release --project src/Sindri/Aw.Sindri.Host --); the test points it at a stub.
# AW_SINDRI_CMD=

# scripts/install-tldraw.sh (setup.sh): where the Linux tldraw offline AppImage goes (default ~/.local/share/tldraw-offline).
# AW_TLDRAW_DIR=
# scripts/install-tldraw.sh: where the Linux `tldraw-offline` launcher link goes (default ~/.local/bin).
# AW_TLDRAW_BIN_DIR=
# scripts/install-tldraw.sh: the macOS app bundle it looks for (default "/Applications/tldraw offline.app").
# AW_TLDRAW_APP=
# scripts/install-tldraw.sh: the release download base (default the pinned GitHub release; tests use a file:// dir).
# AW_TLDRAW_URL_BASE=
# scripts/install-tldraw.sh: test-only overrides. AW_TLDRAW_SHA256 replaces the arch's pinned sha256 (a stand-in AppImage);
# AW_TLDRAW_ARCH fakes `uname -m`.
# AW_TLDRAW_SHA256=
# AW_TLDRAW_ARCH=
